(2158257, 291022, 50205, '<td valign="top">thanks a lot everybody!</td>', 'thanks a lot everybody!', '2006-02-17 01:32:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2158520, 290902, 30364, '<td valign="top">There''s a beautiful woman trapped in there, Lev.  I see her right eye, just to the right and above centre.  I see a garland of flowers in her hair.  I see her raised upper arm, starting left centre and extending up through the top of the frame.  And I see her breasts at lower centre and right (well, OK, I <i>always</i> see breasts).  And now that I''ve found her, I cannot look at this image and see anything else.<br/>This is a beautiful series of photographs ... well conceived, flawlessly executed and beautifully processed.  Oh, and the titles are a final sublime touch.</td>', 'There''s a beautiful woman trapped in there, Lev.  I see her right eye, just to the right and above centre.  I see a garland of flowers in her hair.  I see her raised upper arm, starting left centre and extending up through the top of the frame.  And I see her breasts at lower centre and right (well, OK, I always see breasts).  And now that I''ve found her, I cannot look at this image and see anything else.This is a beautiful series of photographs ... well conceived, flawlessly executed and beautifully processed.  Oh, and the titles are a final sublime touch.', '2006-02-17 06:59:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2158884, 291848, 49480, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><i>In the future, it''s very helpful for the critiquer if you comment on your picture (look in the CC forum).  It''s hard to give suggestions when we don''t know what you were shooting for, etc...</i> <br/> <br/><u>Composition:</u> <br/>I like the angle of the subject since it presents diagonal lines leading the eye into the picture.  <br/> <br/><u>Lighting and Technique:</u> <br/>I''m confused by the small aperture, long shutter speed, and small DOF.  In any case, the lighting on this is a little strange since the reflections on the corners of the shapes draw my attention to the reflection instead of to the subject.  <br/> <br/><u>Post-Processing:</u> <br/>Sharpening looks good, brightness and contrast are good.  <br/> <br/><u>Suggestions/Improvements:</u> <br/>   The small DOF effectively locks my eye to the center of the picture but there''s no real interest there.  If you had made the DOF a little larger so the OOF areas gradually going out of focus I think this would''ve worked better.  <br/>   It''s hard to tell what this was lit with (looks like a ring flash or a ceiling fan), but I think bouncing a flash to get a diffused source would''ve helped prevent the distracting reflections.<br/> <br/>I hope this was useful to you, and please feel free to contact me via PM if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Zeke Smith<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-17 11:08:05.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  In the future, it''s very helpful for the critiquer if you comment on your picture (look in the CC forum).  It''s hard to give suggestions when we don''t know what you were shooting for, etc...  Composition: I like the angle of the subject since it presents diagonal lines leading the eye into the picture.   Lighting and Technique: I''m confused by the small aperture, long shutter speed, and small DOF.  In any case, the lighting on this is a little strange since the reflections on the corners of the shapes draw my attention to the reflection instead of to the subject.   Post-Processing: Sharpening looks good, brightness and contrast are good.   Suggestions/Improvements:    The small DOF effectively locks my eye to the center of the picture but there''s no real interest there.  If you had made the DOF a little larger so the OOF areas gradually going out of focus I think this would''ve worked better.     It''s hard to tell what this was lit with (looks like a ring flash or a ceiling fan), but I think bouncing a flash to get a diffused source would''ve helped prevent the distracting reflections. I hope this was useful to you, and please feel free to contact me via PM if you have any questions regarding this critique. Regards,Zeke Smith', '2006-02-17 11:04:43.000000', '2006-02-17 11:08:05.000000', 0),
(2159146, 291699, 5728, '<td valign="top">Hey Brett, a fellow Kiwi reporting in for a rare Critique Club showing. However, after reading your CC comment on DrAchoo''s photo I reckon you could do a better job on critiquing your own photo :) I won''t go as deeply into it as you do though.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your second highest scorer so far. I would say this image was a little underrated, I would have placed it a bit higher than 79th. There was a lot of competition to fight against in this challenge though. It was a good choice for the challenge, very abstract and not easy to guess what it is. The title fits well, as it does resemble molten matter in a way. The blue tones from the reflections are all that determine this is not a B&amp;W photo, and do add to the image, although a little deeper/saturated could have brought in more impact. There is not really too much to comment on an image like this which probably explains why you didn''t receive too many comment on it.<br/> <br/>Overall though technically well done but there is just that little something missing to give it that extra kick to make an outstanding image out of a good image.</td>', 'Hey Brett, a fellow Kiwi reporting in for a rare Critique Club showing. However, after reading your CC comment on DrAchoo''s photo I reckon you could do a better job on critiquing your own photo :) I won''t go as deeply into it as you do though. Congratulations on your second highest scorer so far. I would say this image was a little underrated, I would have placed it a bit higher than 79th. There was a lot of competition to fight against in this challenge though. It was a good choice for the challenge, very abstract and not easy to guess what it is. The title fits well, as it does resemble molten matter in a way. The blue tones from the reflections are all that determine this is not a B&W photo, and do add to the image, although a little deeper/saturated could have brought in more impact. There is not really too much to comment on an image like this which probably explains why you didn''t receive too many comment on it. Overall though technically well done but there is just that little something missing to give it that extra kick to make an outstanding image out of a good image.', '2006-02-17 12:59:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2159400, 290902, 30214, '<td valign="top">Your imagination surely beats mine, Paul. I just saw a few funny creatures and plants, but I knew there must be a woman there somewhere, just could not see her. Thanks for revealing her for me! :)<br/> <br/>[Actually, I thought this was the least erotic photo from the series. Now I am not so sure...]<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-17 15:53:39.</i></td>', 'Your imagination surely beats mine, Paul. I just saw a few funny creatures and plants, but I knew there must be a woman there somewhere, just could not see her. Thanks for revealing her for me! :) [Actually, I thought this was the least erotic photo from the series. Now I am not so sure...]', '2006-02-17 15:50:33.000000', '2006-02-17 15:53:39.000000', 0),
(2159769, 291824, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique club. I think your photo really meets the challenge well. Its definatly an abstract. I like the colors and the lines. I think you scored really well, there are a few suggestions that I might suggest to help you fix the problems I see with it. The light? reflection in the upper left likely should have been cloned out and made the photo super smooth. I also would have tried to clone out the bubbles that have the reflections in them. I am kind of surprised at the lack of comments you got. Thats kind of surprising for a photo to finish with an above average score and not get comments. I think overall you did very good with a few tweaks to the post processing it likely would have scored even better. Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique club. I think your photo really meets the challenge well. Its definatly an abstract. I like the colors and the lines. I think you scored really well, there are a few suggestions that I might suggest to help you fix the problems I see with it. The light? reflection in the upper left likely should have been cloned out and made the photo super smooth. I also would have tried to clone out the bubbles that have the reflections in them. I am kind of surprised at the lack of comments you got. Thats kind of surprising for a photo to finish with an above average score and not get comments. I think overall you did very good with a few tweaks to the post processing it likely would have scored even better. Good luck in future challenges.', '2006-02-17 20:09:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2160435, 290508, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Foliage" is an excellent addition into the Abstract challenge, and I am very glad to see you finished in the top 10%.  Just thumbing through the challenge I remember this thumbnail sticking out.  The frame is so full and bright it demands attention. The detail of this close up is amazing.  The little spider enhances this shot, it is what clued me into what the shot was of.  I think when voters have to stop and try and figure out what we are looking at is a prefect fit for an abstract.  The contrasting colors of the leaves give so much depth as opposed to leaves that were just one color.  Also the edges separate the image from a boring run of the mill close up.  Personally I don''t see anything I would change or recommend trying.  I personally would be extremely proud of this piece if I were you.  Good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Foliage" is an excellent addition into the Abstract challenge, and I am very glad to see you finished in the top 10%.  Just thumbing through the challenge I remember this thumbnail sticking out.  The frame is so full and bright it demands attention. The detail of this close up is amazing.  The little spider enhances this shot, it is what clued me into what the shot was of.  I think when voters have to stop and try and figure out what we are looking at is a prefect fit for an abstract.  The contrasting colors of the leaves give so much depth as opposed to leaves that were just one color.  Also the edges separate the image from a boring run of the mill close up.  Personally I don''t see anything I would change or recommend trying.  I personally would be extremely proud of this piece if I were you.  Good work.', '2006-02-18 01:36:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2160455, 291218, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Circles Of Colour" is a nice photo to have used for the Abstract challenge.  I think when voters have to stop and think of what this is actual a shot of, then you have met the challenge.  <br/> <br/>The colors you chose are very bright and vibrant.  I still am not sure what the shot is actually of so good job, it is defiantly abstract.  I would be interested to see the shot if you were able to include the full circle, it just seems a little cropped. It would also be interesting to see the center a little clearer, but that''s just my opinion.  Excellent work and use of color.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Circles Of Colour" is a nice photo to have used for the Abstract challenge.  I think when voters have to stop and think of what this is actual a shot of, then you have met the challenge.   The colors you chose are very bright and vibrant.  I still am not sure what the shot is actually of so good job, it is defiantly abstract.  I would be interested to see the shot if you were able to include the full circle, it just seems a little cropped. It would also be interesting to see the center a little clearer, but that''s just my opinion.  Excellent work and use of color.', '2006-02-18 01:46:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2160469, 291022, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"The Human Soul (female)" is a unique piece, the title defiantly grabbed my attention.  It was an excellent out of the box idea and shot.  During the challenge I was very curious to see what this actually was, and now I am still quite surprised.  The abstract part of the challenge is prefect, I am thinking that maybe it was the empty space at the top the hurt the score.  I think abstractly speaking your placement and emptiness of the top is a great fit but maybe from the voters perspective it seemed a little off because we are used to see full centered shots.  I think you did great work capturing the glow with altering it to much or creating noise.  I would be interested to see a few different crops to enhance the subject, but I still Iike your choice.  I will be really curious to see your future pieces. Good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "The Human Soul (female)" is a unique piece, the title defiantly grabbed my attention.  It was an excellent out of the box idea and shot.  During the challenge I was very curious to see what this actually was, and now I am still quite surprised.  The abstract part of the challenge is prefect, I am thinking that maybe it was the empty space at the top the hurt the score.  I think abstractly speaking your placement and emptiness of the top is a great fit but maybe from the voters perspective it seemed a little off because we are used to see full centered shots.  I think you did great work capturing the glow with altering it to much or creating noise.  I would be interested to see a few different crops to enhance the subject, but I still Iike your choice.  I will be really curious to see your future pieces. Good work.', '2006-02-18 01:53:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2160596, 288203, 38508, '<td valign="top">eeeuhm...... I don''t get it!<br/>But sure a great picture!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'eeeuhm...... I don''t get it!But sure a great picture!! ', '2006-02-18 04:54:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2161565, 291629, 5112, '<td valign="top">A pink and black balloon!  Beautiful.  One thing that comes to mind though is that it might have been interesting to go closer just a bit more, and make sure that all four corner have the same colour (black I think would work best).  The little pieces at the side edges (especially at left) take away from the overall graphic abstractness.</td>', 'A pink and black balloon!  Beautiful.  One thing that comes to mind though is that it might have been interesting to go closer just a bit more, and make sure that all four corner have the same colour (black I think would work best).  The little pieces at the side edges (especially at left) take away from the overall graphic abstractness.', '2006-02-18 15:41:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2161602, 291436, 49480, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club.</b> <br/> <br/>Keep in mind, when asking for critiques (the check box when you submit your picture) you should provide comments so the reviewer knows what you were trying to get from your shot.<br/> <br/><u>Composition:</u> <br/>This shot has great potential...the leading lines of the keys draw the eyes into the picture.<br/> <br/><u>Camera Work &amp; Technique:</u> <br/>FOCUS...You''ll hear this a thousand times when there''s not something in focus in your image.  Keep the viewer interested by having something in focus and using OOF areas to keep their eyes where you want them.  Try and prevent highlights from blowing out as well.  <br/> <br/><u>Suggestions:</u> <br/>Only thing to say here is to get your picture in focus.  Abstract challenges are usually won by interesting colors and shapes that don''t necessarily make the viewer see a larger picture...just appreciating the image.  Good luck.  I hope this review has been helpful.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  Keep in mind, when asking for critiques (the check box when you submit your picture) you should provide comments so the reviewer knows what you were trying to get from your shot. Composition: This shot has great potential...the leading lines of the keys draw the eyes into the picture. Camera Work & Technique: FOCUS...You''ll hear this a thousand times when there''s not something in focus in your image.  Keep the viewer interested by having something in focus and using OOF areas to keep their eyes where you want them.  Try and prevent highlights from blowing out as well.   Suggestions: Only thing to say here is to get your picture in focus.  Abstract challenges are usually won by interesting colors and shapes that don''t necessarily make the viewer see a larger picture...just appreciating the image.  Good luck.  I hope this review has been helpful.', '2006-02-18 16:19:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2161796, 291266, 53550, '<td valign="top">I like it, it does make me think of heat, congrats.</td>', 'I like it, it does make me think of heat, congrats.', '2006-02-18 18:27:45.000000', NULL, 0),
