(2163238, 291794, 27763, '<td valign="top">Nice photo that stands out from the pack.  I never would have figured this out if you hadn''t explained it!</td>', 'Nice photo that stands out from the pack.  I never would have figured this out if you hadn''t explained it!', '2006-02-19 12:40:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163381, 291665, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>How do you touch base on the technical aspects of an abstract?  Tough one.<br/>I will say that I love the color, the way that the slight variations of the color flow through the photo is nice, I like the background with the forground colors  and I think the soft focus works really well to create an abstract feel.<br/>Placement of the subject (curved line) is great.  Not dead center, but off center works really well to create some visual appeal.<br/>I think with abstracts, you gotta go mostly with visual appeal, and to me, this photo has just that.  I really love the colors and the overall feel and flow of the image.<br/>Not really much to add, due to your lack of photographer''s comments, I am not really sure what you personally were going for, so I wouldn''t be able to tell you if you succeeded in YOUR goal, but the image is appealing.<br/>~Heather~</td>', '*Critique Club* How do you touch base on the technical aspects of an abstract?  Tough one.I will say that I love the color, the way that the slight variations of the color flow through the photo is nice, I like the background with the forground colors  and I think the soft focus works really well to create an abstract feel.Placement of the subject (curved line) is great.  Not dead center, but off center works really well to create some visual appeal.I think with abstracts, you gotta go mostly with visual appeal, and to me, this photo has just that.  I really love the colors and the overall feel and flow of the image.Not really much to add, due to your lack of photographer''s comments, I am not really sure what you personally were going for, so I wouldn''t be able to tell you if you succeeded in YOUR goal, but the image is appealing.~Heather~', '2006-02-19 14:17:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163403, 290405, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Without any photographer''s comments on this, i can only offer my critique based on personal opinion alone, since I have no clue what you were trying to accomplish with this photo.<br/>That being said, I think it''s an interesting abstract.  Someone suggested that it may be a cactus, but I don''t see that.  I see something metal here.  Not sure what, but somethig metal.<br/>The colors are neat, and the lines add something to the photo, but for me, it lacks something that really makes it pop.  It''s hard to give technical review on an abstract, but I see your focus is good, and the angle of the object isn''t boring, but still lacking something for me.  Overall, nice colors, focus and angle.<br/>~Heather~<br/> <br/>Edit to add that I saw your Alien Remnants photo and THAT one really stands out to me.  I much prefer that one.  I like the lines, the color and that one holds my interest much much more than this one does.  More to look at, I think.  <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-19 14:26:04.</i></td>', '*Critique Club* Without any photographer''s comments on this, i can only offer my critique based on personal opinion alone, since I have no clue what you were trying to accomplish with this photo.That being said, I think it''s an interesting abstract.  Someone suggested that it may be a cactus, but I don''t see that.  I see something metal here.  Not sure what, but somethig metal.The colors are neat, and the lines add something to the photo, but for me, it lacks something that really makes it pop.  It''s hard to give technical review on an abstract, but I see your focus is good, and the angle of the object isn''t boring, but still lacking something for me.  Overall, nice colors, focus and angle.~Heather~ Edit to add that I saw your Alien Remnants photo and THAT one really stands out to me.  I much prefer that one.  I like the lines, the color and that one holds my interest much much more than this one does.  More to look at, I think.  ', '2006-02-19 14:23:55.000000', '2006-02-19 14:26:04.000000', 0),
(2163427, 288203, 5728, '<td valign="top">A few more details would be good to find out what this actually is.</td>', 'A few more details would be good to find out what this actually is.', '2006-02-19 14:27:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163429, 290146, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Definately abstract.  I think I could have guessed what this was, especially with the title, so maybe a little lose on the challenge, but still abstract non the less.<br/>The color is nice.  The photo is just not holding my attention much.  I think that the area in the lower right appears to be the main focal point, since that''s where all the lines are drawing my attention to, and that area lacks visual appeal.  It''s hard to critique the technical aspects of an abstract, but your focus looks good.  I wonder what this would be like with a soft focus?  Maybe give it a more abstract feel or add something of interest?<br/>Overall, I think it''s very representative of an abstract, but lacking something that really holds my interest.<br/>~Heather~</td>', '*Critique Club* Definately abstract.  I think I could have guessed what this was, especially with the title, so maybe a little lose on the challenge, but still abstract non the less.The color is nice.  The photo is just not holding my attention much.  I think that the area in the lower right appears to be the main focal point, since that''s where all the lines are drawing my attention to, and that area lacks visual appeal.  It''s hard to critique the technical aspects of an abstract, but your focus looks good.  I wonder what this would be like with a soft focus?  Maybe give it a more abstract feel or add something of interest?Overall, I think it''s very representative of an abstract, but lacking something that really holds my interest.~Heather~', '2006-02-19 14:31:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163437, 291765, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This photo is very busy.  Definately abstract, but not that attractive to me.<br/>The colors don''t seem like the pop as much as I would like them to.  The red is nice and vibrant, but the yellow is just kind of dull.  I think that if the yellows stood out more against the red, that it would help to add some visual appeal.<br/>It''s hard to critique the technical aspects of an abstract, especially with the lack of phtoographer''s comments, I can really only offer my opinion since I don''t know for sure what your intentions were with this photo.<br/>If I were to guess, I think this would be a blown glass paperweight or something similar.<br/>It''s interesting, but just doesn''t hold my attention long.<br/>~Heather~</td>', '*Critique Club* This photo is very busy.  Definately abstract, but not that attractive to me.The colors don''t seem like the pop as much as I would like them to.  The red is nice and vibrant, but the yellow is just kind of dull.  I think that if the yellows stood out more against the red, that it would help to add some visual appeal.It''s hard to critique the technical aspects of an abstract, especially with the lack of phtoographer''s comments, I can really only offer my opinion since I don''t know for sure what your intentions were with this photo.If I were to guess, I think this would be a blown glass paperweight or something similar.It''s interesting, but just doesn''t hold my attention long.~Heather~', '2006-02-19 14:38:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163577, 291605, 49480, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>Please remember to leave comments when you request a critique.  Without them, it''s very hard to tell what you were trying for and makes a critique very difficult.<br/> <br/><u>Composition:</u> <br/>There doesn''t seem to be any real subject of this shot and what''s in focus tends to take my eye out of the image (the round thing on the right).  The orange area in the bottom left is also distracting since the rest of the image is this soft peach color.<br/> <br/><u>Camera Work &amp; Technique:</u> <br/>Focus is good.  DOF is quite small and doesn''t seem to serve a purpose for being so small.  The in focus areas don''t attract my attention.  Lighting looks good with no hot spots.<br/> <br/><u>Post-processing:</u> <br/>It''s hard to tell but it looks like the saturation may have been bumped up too much since there seems to be sections where the color changes abruptly in the top left.  That may not be true but with the limited DOF it''s hard to tell what''s going on up there (and without knowing the post-processing steps so please include them in the future).<br/> <br/><u>Suggestions:</u> <br/>You''ve got this nice diagonal line coming from the top that would be great coming from the top-left corner.  Try and keep in focus areas away from the edge of the shot as they lead the eye out of the image.  Moving the subject a little to the left in the image would''ve helped this out a lot.  Increasing the DOF some so that we can see the extent of the shape also would''ve given the subject more interest.<br/> <br/>I hope you find this critique helpful.  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Zeke Smith</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Please remember to leave comments when you request a critique.  Without them, it''s very hard to tell what you were trying for and makes a critique very difficult. Composition: There doesn''t seem to be any real subject of this shot and what''s in focus tends to take my eye out of the image (the round thing on the right).  The orange area in the bottom left is also distracting since the rest of the image is this soft peach color. Camera Work & Technique: Focus is good.  DOF is quite small and doesn''t seem to serve a purpose for being so small.  The in focus areas don''t attract my attention.  Lighting looks good with no hot spots. Post-processing: It''s hard to tell but it looks like the saturation may have been bumped up too much since there seems to be sections where the color changes abruptly in the top left.  That may not be true but with the limited DOF it''s hard to tell what''s going on up there (and without knowing the post-processing steps so please include them in the future). Suggestions: You''ve got this nice diagonal line coming from the top that would be great coming from the top-left corner.  Try and keep in focus areas away from the edge of the shot as they lead the eye out of the image.  Moving the subject a little to the left in the image would''ve helped this out a lot.  Increasing the DOF some so that we can see the extent of the shape also would''ve given the subject more interest. I hope you find this critique helpful.  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions. Regards,Zeke Smith', '2006-02-19 16:08:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163677, 288753, 30982, '<td valign="top">12th ain''t average.  :-)<br/> <br/>Obviously a well-done shot - neat to find out what it was!</td>', '12th ain''t average.  :-) Obviously a well-done shot - neat to find out what it was!', '2006-02-19 16:54:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163770, 291480, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Blown Energy" is a nice fit into the abstract challenge, it is a different and unusual piece.  After reading your deception I would have never guessed that this is how you create the image (very good thinking).<br/> <br/>The image is self is overall pleasing.  Nice use of contrasting colors to grab the viewers attention.  The flow of the image is nice and pleasing to the eye to go from the left to the right.  I also like the grainy appearance of the the light in comparison to the smooth glass in the upper part.  I have noticed sometimes people will vote lower because of a grain not realizing it was put there internationally.  Good use of a black background instead of trying to put another color into the shot.  I think the idea and implementation of Blown Energy was a really good idea, maybe it just not as appealing to voters as some of the other images.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Blown Energy" is a nice fit into the abstract challenge, it is a different and unusual piece.  After reading your deception I would have never guessed that this is how you create the image (very good thinking). The image is self is overall pleasing.  Nice use of contrasting colors to grab the viewers attention.  The flow of the image is nice and pleasing to the eye to go from the left to the right.  I also like the grainy appearance of the the light in comparison to the smooth glass in the upper part.  I have noticed sometimes people will vote lower because of a grain not realizing it was put there internationally.  Good use of a black background instead of trying to put another color into the shot.  I think the idea and implementation of Blown Energy was a really good idea, maybe it just not as appealing to voters as some of the other images.', '2006-02-19 18:06:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163778, 291190, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>I''m not sure what this is so it certainly quilifies as an abstract :)<br/>The composition is good but there is something about the color... the pink and blue on the window bothers me a little bit. I think this picture would  look much better in bw. I''ve been looking at your portfolio and you got some really good photos. Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Critique Club:I''m not sure what this is so it certainly quilifies as an abstract :)The composition is good but there is something about the color... the pink and blue on the window bothers me a little bit. I think this picture would  look much better in bw. I''ve been looking at your portfolio and you got some really good photos. Keep up the good work.', '2006-02-19 18:13:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163786, 290766, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>The focus is just spot on. And this green color is just beautiful. And green really goes with red. The negative space adds to the picture. There is nothing that I would have done different on this shot. Good job.<br/> <br/>Your portfolio is really good. You''ve got some really good pictures. Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Critique Club:The focus is just spot on. And this green color is just beautiful. And green really goes with red. The negative space adds to the picture. There is nothing that I would have done different on this shot. Good job. Your portfolio is really good. You''ve got some really good pictures. Keep up the good work.', '2006-02-19 18:17:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163790, 288627, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>It certainly is abstract :) I think a black background would have been perfect in this shot. And a bit more contrast. This is a fun shot and a bit different. I like the motion in it. Good luck and keep up the good job.</td>', 'Critique Club:It certainly is abstract :) I think a black background would have been perfect in this shot. And a bit more contrast. This is a fun shot and a bit different. I like the motion in it. Good luck and keep up the good job.', '2006-02-19 18:19:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163796, 291815, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>People probably scored it lower because they recognized the spoon. I think the waves in the cloth at the top of the shot are cool. They add to the round shape of the spoon. The contrast in the picture is good as well. Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Critique Club:People probably scored it lower because they recognized the spoon. I think the waves in the cloth at the top of the shot are cool. They add to the round shape of the spoon. The contrast in the picture is good as well. Keep up the good work.', '2006-02-19 18:21:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163800, 290126, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>Heill og sæll. Held að þessi hefði verið betri í svart/hvítu að mínu mati. Það er fín hugmynd að nota vatn í svona en það er eitthvað sem vantar. Spurning hvort það hefði verið betra að fara dálítið nær vatninu. En svart/hvítt og meiri contrast er eitthvað sem ég held að myndi gera þessa mynd betri.</td>', 'Critique Club:Heill og sæll. Held að þessi hefði verið betri í svart/hvítu að mínu mati. Það er fín hugmynd að nota vatn í svona en það er eitthvað sem vantar. Spurning hvort það hefði verið betra að fara dálítið nær vatninu. En svart/hvítt og meiri contrast er eitthvað sem ég held að myndi gera þessa mynd betri.', '2006-02-19 18:25:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163801, 289699, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>Great lighting. The perfect white background looks good. I really like the symetry of it. Good job!</td>', 'Critique Club:Great lighting. The perfect white background looks good. I really like the symetry of it. Good job!', '2006-02-19 18:25:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163803, 291845, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"A-Zebra" is a nice close up.  In the abstract challenge I think was looking for the unusual I really liked images you really couldn''t tell what they were, but I remind myself how very different people envision a subject.  You have made a very unusual shot with probably household items, good work.<br/> <br/>The image itself is a nice clean shot. I like your use of black and white, I would be curious to see the complete image in black and white.  The lighting is also interesting, possibly a flash and maybe some other lighting. I think the shot might have been interesting from some different perspectives, it just seems a little to centered or focused on the center subject.  I think you do great work with objects and your depth of field, I think it just didn''t work as well for you in this challenge (I had to peek at your other work, which has some amazing photos).  <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "A-Zebra" is a nice close up.  In the abstract challenge I think was looking for the unusual I really liked images you really couldn''t tell what they were, but I remind myself how very different people envision a subject.  You have made a very unusual shot with probably household items, good work. The image itself is a nice clean shot. I like your use of black and white, I would be curious to see the complete image in black and white.  The lighting is also interesting, possibly a flash and maybe some other lighting. I think the shot might have been interesting from some different perspectives, it just seems a little to centered or focused on the center subject.  I think you do great work with objects and your depth of field, I think it just didn''t work as well for you in this challenge (I had to peek at your other work, which has some amazing photos).  ', '2006-02-19 18:27:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163836, 291609, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Planetary" is a very attention grabbing piece with its bright red center.   This is a nice addition to the Abstract challenge.  Looking at this shot, I wasn''t quite sure what it was, which makes it fit into the abstract even more for me.<br/> <br/>The image itself defiantly could use to be bigger, I sometimes have a hard time with the resizing, but the closest you can get it too be to the 150 the better.  I think if you were able to submit a higher quality shot the image itself might have looked clearer and scored higher. After looking at a few of your other shots maybe it is the resolution on the camera.  Well regardless of that this shot was a nice and different entry to see.  I like the overall placement of the focus and composition.  Good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Planetary" is a very attention grabbing piece with its bright red center.   This is a nice addition to the Abstract challenge.  Looking at this shot, I wasn''t quite sure what it was, which makes it fit into the abstract even more for me. The image itself defiantly could use to be bigger, I sometimes have a hard time with the resizing, but the closest you can get it too be to the 150 the better.  I think if you were able to submit a higher quality shot the image itself might have looked clearer and scored higher. After looking at a few of your other shots maybe it is the resolution on the camera.  Well regardless of that this shot was a nice and different entry to see.  I like the overall placement of the focus and composition.  Good work.', '2006-02-19 18:39:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163861, 291352, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Eye of the Machine" is an excellent addition to Abstract challenge.  I am really surprised it didn''t place higher.  After reading your description it makes complete sense how you shot this, I would have probably not been able to figure it out.<br/> <br/>The image is so full motion it just grabs your attention.  I think blue was an excellent choice, it leaves the image clean and cool.  I really like how if you look deep down in the center you are able to see something, not just an empty space.  I would be interested in seeing the shot is a prefect square to compliment the circle.  You have done some interesting work, I hope you continue to participate in the challenges.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Eye of the Machine" is an excellent addition to Abstract challenge.  I am really surprised it didn''t place higher.  After reading your description it makes complete sense how you shot this, I would have probably not been able to figure it out. The image is so full motion it just grabs your attention.  I think blue was an excellent choice, it leaves the image clean and cool.  I really like how if you look deep down in the center you are able to see something, not just an empty space.  I would be interested in seeing the shot is a prefect square to compliment the circle.  You have done some interesting work, I hope you continue to participate in the challenges.', '2006-02-19 18:54:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163872, 288287, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Would i?" is an extremely interesting piece in the abstract challenge, I had no idea exactly what it was.  After reading your comments I can see the eye and get the title but during the challenge I completely miss it.<br/> <br/>This is defiantly an abstract piece.  It is almost haunting and enchanting at the same time trying to figure out the image. I am not quit sure what I would recommend because it is so unusual and I am sure you use the blur on purpose to enhance the subject.  Maybe crop the image down and make it tighter for the subject to be the complete focus.  Good out of the box thinking.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Would i?" is an extremely interesting piece in the abstract challenge, I had no idea exactly what it was.  After reading your comments I can see the eye and get the title but during the challenge I completely miss it. This is defiantly an abstract piece.  It is almost haunting and enchanting at the same time trying to figure out the image. I am not quit sure what I would recommend because it is so unusual and I am sure you use the blur on purpose to enhance the subject.  Maybe crop the image down and make it tighter for the subject to be the complete focus.  Good out of the box thinking.', '2006-02-19 19:01:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163900, 291413, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Well top 100 isn''t too bad even though I was sure you would be top 10 or 20.  "Tubes" is a prefect addition to the Abstract challenge.  I really love how fluid and complete this shot feels.<br/> <br/>I would have never guessed during the challenge that this was hair gel, what an excellent use of the resources that you had.  I also think the bubble is a great addition to shot like something is moving through these amazingly clear tubes.  Also I like the use of red for the background.  I wonder if the shot was completely filled with gel and no empty spaces about the background it would have scored higher by others.  I do think the include of the reflection towards the bottom was important to leave in.  Great work.</td>', '*Critique Club* Well top 100 isn''t too bad even though I was sure you would be top 10 or 20.  "Tubes" is a prefect addition to the Abstract challenge.  I really love how fluid and complete this shot feels. I would have never guessed during the challenge that this was hair gel, what an excellent use of the resources that you had.  I also think the bubble is a great addition to shot like something is moving through these amazingly clear tubes.  Also I like the use of red for the background.  I wonder if the shot was completely filled with gel and no empty spaces about the background it would have scored higher by others.  I do think the include of the reflection towards the bottom was important to leave in.  Great work.', '2006-02-19 19:20:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2163918, 290187, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Natural curves" is a great example of abstract, taking something ordinary and creating the unusual out of it.  52nd isn''t too bad of a placement for your first challenge.  The lighting makes this shot amazing, the softness it is able to create.  The use of a t-shirt to create the backdrop, is great.  I doubt many people could make such a nice shot with such basic elements.  Like "beggs" said love the negative space, it really allows the viewer to focus on the subject.  The use of black and red allows the image to stay basic and still look intriguing.  I also like the softness and overall composition of "Natural curves".  This is a very professional looking shot and I could easily see it used in advertisements.  I personally can''t think of anything  I would like to see changed, great work!</td>', '*Critique Club* "Natural curves" is a great example of abstract, taking something ordinary and creating the unusual out of it.  52nd isn''t too bad of a placement for your first challenge.  The lighting makes this shot amazing, the softness it is able to create.  The use of a t-shirt to create the backdrop, is great.  I doubt many people could make such a nice shot with such basic elements.  Like "beggs" said love the negative space, it really allows the viewer to focus on the subject.  The use of black and red allows the image to stay basic and still look intriguing.  I also like the softness and overall composition of "Natural curves".  This is a very professional looking shot and I could easily see it used in advertisements.  I personally can''t think of anything  I would like to see changed, great work!', '2006-02-19 19:31:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2164005, 291553, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>This is almost like an abstract painting. The composition is good. I really like this photo. It is different. The white thick border works well. Good job and good luck in future challanges.</td>', 'Critique Club:This is almost like an abstract painting. The composition is good. I really like this photo. It is different. The white thick border works well. Good job and good luck in future challanges.', '2006-02-19 20:10:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2164010, 289847, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>This looks like and graphic painting or something like that. I see some japanese or chines influences. Looks like something from 1800 something. I like it alot. Good job and good luck in future challanges.</td>', 'Critique Club:This looks like and graphic painting or something like that. I see some japanese or chines influences. Looks like something from 1800 something. I like it alot. Good job and good luck in future challanges.', '2006-02-19 20:12:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2164019, 291097, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>The composition is good but I''m not sure about the post processing. I would like to see this picture with less post processing because the composiiton is good and I think it could be a great picture. Good luck in future challanges. I like your Wild Life II entry alot.</td>', 'Critique Club:The composition is good but I''m not sure about the post processing. I would like to see this picture with less post processing because the composiiton is good and I think it could be a great picture. Good luck in future challanges. I like your Wild Life II entry alot.', '2006-02-19 20:14:40.000000', NULL, 0),
